# Log Analyzer

A small Python tool that reads a server log and flags IP addresses with repeated failed logins. I built it as my first project while learning cybersecurity.

## How it works
The script reads `server.log` line by line. For every failed login, it adds one to that IP's count in a dictionary. Any IP with more than 2 failures is flagged as suspicious and saved to `report.txt`.

## How to run it
    py log_analyzer.py

## What I learned
- How to read and write files in Python
- How dictionaries can count things
- The difference between write mode ("w") and append mode ("a")
- Basic Git: init, add, commit, push

## What broke
- I ran `git init` in my user folder instead of the project folder, so Git tried to stage an Android project. I fixed it by deleting the accidental `.git` folder and starting again in the right place. Now I check my folder with `pwd` before any Git command.
- My file wouldn't save into the folder at first, so I created it from the terminal instead.

